Description: fftools_sched: gate sink-less skip per-output, not per-decoder
 Patch 0120's start_prepare modification skipped the whole-decoder
 dst_finished allocation when `dec->sink_less` was set:
 .
   if (dec->sink_less)
       continue;
 .
 That's correct when the decoder has ONLY a sink-less side-channel
 output (the `-map_inlineass` self-decode case where the binding is
 the only consumer). It's WRONG when the decoder has BOTH a sink-less
 side-channel AND a real OST consumer (the dual-consumer case
 triggered when an argv keeps Plex's `-map <spec> -f null -codec ass
 nullfile` decode-sink alongside `-map_inlineass <spec>`).
 .
 In the dual-consumer case, ist_use() for the OST registers output 0
 with nb_dst=1 (the real OST). Then ist_inlineass_add() runs ist_use()
 idempotently (no new output added) and calls sch_dec_set_sinkless()
 on the SHARED decoder. start_prepare then hits the early `continue`
 and skips allocation of dst_finished for output 0 — even though it
 has a real consumer that needs it. dst_finished stays NULL.
 .
 First sch_dec_send for the OST output dereferences
 `&o->dst_finished[0]` and SEGVs:
 .
   Thread "dec1:0:srt" SIGSEGV at fftools/ffmpeg_sched.c:2318
     #0  sch_dec_send (sch, dec_idx=<opt>, out_idx=<opt>, frame)
         o = {dst=0x..., dst_finished=0x0, nb_dst=1}  <-- bug
     #1  process_subtitle  (fftools/ffmpeg_dec.c:618)
     #2  transcode_subtitles  (fftools/ffmpeg_dec.c:707)
     #3  packet_decode  (fftools/ffmpeg_dec.c:717)
     #4  decoder_thread  (fftools/ffmpeg_dec.c:966)
 .
 Live-validated 2026-05-26 on plex-test with the minimal repro:
 .
   ffmpeg -f lavfi -i 'color=...' -i sidecar.srt \
          -map_inlineass 1:s:0 -filter_complex '[0:v]inlineass=...[v]' \
          -map [v] -c:v libx264 -f null - \
          -map 1:s:0 -f null -codec ass nullfile
 .
 Fix: move the sink-less check INTO the per-output loop. For outputs
 that are genuinely sink-less (nb_dst == 0), treat the "not connected
 to any sink" as a valid state and skip allocation. For outputs that
 DO have downstream consumers, allocate dst_finished as normal.
 .
 The sink_less DECODER flag remains as-is (used by sch_dec_send's
 nb_dst==0 fallthrough guard and unchoke_downstream's NULL-deref
 guard); only the start_prepare validation+alloc loop changes.
Origin: scaleplex; refines 0120
Forwarded: not-needed
Author: scaleplex
Last-Update: 2026-05-26
--- a/fftools/ffmpeg_sched.c
+++ b/fftools/ffmpeg_sched.c
@@ -1514,15 +1514,20 @@ static int start_prepare(Scheduler *sch)
             return AVERROR(EINVAL);
         }

-        /* scaleplex: a sink-less decoder feeds a side-channel, not a
-         * scheduler output; its auto-created output 0 stays unconnected. */
-        if (dec->sink_less)
-            continue;
-
         for (unsigned j = 0; j < dec->nb_outputs; j++) {
             SchDecOutput *o = &dec->outputs[j];

             if (!o->nb_dst) {
+                /* scaleplex (0122): unconnected output is OK on a sink-less
+                 * decoder — it's the auto-created side-channel output
+                 * that the vf_inlineass binding (or any other side-channel
+                 * consumer) decodes through without a scheduler-tracked
+                 * sink. Leave dst_finished NULL: sch_dec_send's nb_dst==0
+                 * guard (patch 0120) discards frames before reaching the
+                 * loop that would dereference it. Only an unconnected
+                 * output on a NON-sinkless decoder is a real error. */
+                if (dec->sink_less)
+                    continue;
                 av_log(dec, AV_LOG_ERROR,
                        "Decoder output %u not connected to any sink\n", j);
                 return AVERROR(EINVAL);
